\
Selected Playlist to iPod\
\
This script will add the selected playlist and all songs therein to an iPod. It will first test to ensure there is enough room on the iPod, and if there is not, it will let you know how much room is needed to put the particular playlist on the iPod.\
\
Instructions for use: \
\
OS 9: place the script in the "Scripts" folder in the iTunes folder in "Documents."\
\
OSX: Place the script in the "Scripts" folder in "iTunes" in "Library" in "Home." In some cases you might need to create a "Scripts" folder. Make sure your iPod is plugged in to your computer and visible in the iTunes "Sources" window. Select the script from the scripts menu and wait. \
\
Compatability: It's been tested in OS 9.2.3 and OSX 10.1. It requires iTunes 2.0.3 It requires an iPod.\
